1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,192
How does a seller with no website take a card payment?

2
00:00:03,242 --> 00:00:05,832
Many small sellers take orders in a messenger.

3
00:00:05,882 --> 00:00:10,008
A buyer writes, the seller answers, and they agree on a price.

4
00:00:10,058 --> 00:00:12,912
The seller has no checkout and no website code.

5
00:00:12,962 --> 00:00:18,312
Writing a server, sealing requests and managing retries is out of reach.

6
00:00:18,362 --> 00:00:20,976
But sending a link in a chat is easy.

7
00:00:21,026 --> 00:00:22,896
The link still has to be safe.

8
00:00:22,946 --> 00:00:25,080
It must open the real bank page.

9
00:00:25,130 --> 00:00:27,744
It must belong to a website the bank has checked.

10
00:00:27,794 --> 00:00:29,616
It must work only for a while.

11
00:00:29,666 --> 00:00:33,000
And its secret must not be readable from the bank's records.

12
00:00:33,050 --> 00:00:36,216
Think of a paper bill with a pay here button printed on it.

13
00:00:36,266 --> 00:00:40,104
The seller writes the amount and what it is for, and hands it over.

14
00:00:40,154 --> 00:00:42,696
The buyer presses the button and pays.

15
00:00:42,746 --> 00:00:44,688
A payment link is that bill.

16
00:00:44,738 --> 00:00:48,600
A merchant admin or operator makes one in the merchant portal.

17
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:51,216
They pick one of the merchant's live websites.

18
00:00:51,266 --> 00:00:55,584
They write the amount, what the buyer pays for, and how long the link works.

19
00:00:55,634 --> 00:00:58,056
Behind the link is an ordinary payment.

20
00:00:58,106 --> 00:01:02,616
It simply has no API client, because no server created it.

21
00:01:02,666 --> 00:01:06,984
And it has no return address, because there is no shop page to go back to.

22
00:01:07,034 --> 00:01:09,024
Everything else is the same.

23
00:01:09,074 --> 00:01:11,208
The website's own limits still apply.

24
00:01:11,258 --> 00:01:14,136
The website's fee still applies.

25
00:01:14,186 --> 00:01:20,184
The link is the bank's page address with a one-time page token, just like the link a merchant's server receives.

26
00:01:20,234 --> 00:01:23,016
The bank keeps only a fingerprint of that token.

27
00:01:23,066 --> 00:01:26,424
So the full link is shown once, at the moment it is made.

28
00:01:26,474 --> 00:01:30,816
The merchant chooses how long it works, up to the bank's chosen maximum.

29
00:01:30,866 --> 00:01:36,048
The buyer pays on the same bank page as any other payment, with the same card frame.

30
00:01:36,098 --> 00:01:39,576
And a link nobody pays in time is closed as expired.

31
00:01:39,626 --> 00:01:41,448
Now watch the product.

32
00:01:41,498 --> 00:01:44,256
In the merchant portal, open payment links.

33
00:01:44,306 --> 00:01:50,328
The page says it plainly: sell in a chat, and send a buyer a link to the bank's payment page.

34
00:01:50,378 --> 00:01:51,480
Press new link.

35
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:53,760
The form asks for a live website.

36
00:01:53,810 --> 00:01:59,400
If none of the merchant's websites takes payments yet, the form says so, and nothing can be made.

37
00:01:59,450 --> 00:02:02,928
Pick a website, type what the buyer pays for, and the amount.

38
00:02:02,978 --> 00:02:05,016
Choose how many hours the link works.

39
00:02:05,066 --> 00:02:08,568
Ask for longer than the bank allows, and the bank refuses it.

40
00:02:08,618 --> 00:02:10,440
Press create.

41
00:02:10,490 --> 00:02:12,600
A window says your link is ready.

42
00:02:12,650 --> 00:02:17,760
It explains that the link is shown only once, and the bank keeps only its fingerprint.

43
00:02:17,810 --> 00:02:20,160
Press copy link, and it says copied.

44
00:02:20,210 --> 00:02:22,032
Paste it into the chat.

45
00:02:22,082 --> 00:02:26,280
Back on the list, the new link waits for the buyer, without its address.

46
00:02:26,330 --> 00:02:30,864
A teammate who only views can see this list, but has no new link button.

47
00:02:30,914 --> 00:02:32,376
Now switch to the buyer.

48
00:02:32,426 --> 00:02:34,536
The buyer taps the link in the chat.

49
00:02:34,586 --> 00:02:39,480
The same secure bank page opens, with the website, what it is for, and the amount.

50
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:43,080
The buyer pays through the card frame, and the page says paid.

51
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:46,800
There is no back to the shop link, because there is no shop page.

52
00:02:46,850 --> 00:02:49,368
In the portal, the link now shows paid.

53
00:02:49,418 --> 00:02:52,176
Leave another link unpaid past its time.

54
00:02:52,226 --> 00:02:56,928
It turns expired, and a buyer who opens it sees that the link has expired.

55
00:02:56,978 --> 00:02:58,800
What does this protect?

56
00:02:58,850 --> 00:03:03,432
It gives sellers without a website the same safe page as everyone else.

57
00:03:03,482 --> 00:03:06,384
The card never touches the chat or the seller.

58
00:03:06,434 --> 00:03:09,936
A leaked copy of the bank's records holds no working links.

59
00:03:09,986 --> 00:03:15,624
And the website's limits still guard every link, so a link cannot become a back door.

60
00:03:15,674 --> 00:03:17,496
So back to the bill.

61
00:03:17,546 --> 00:03:21,192
A bill with a button, and the same bank page behind it.

62
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:23,112
Next: giving money back.
